public class Solution {
    public boolean isPowerOfThree(int n) {
        // If n is less than or equal to 0, it cannot be a power of 3
        if (n <= 0) {
            return false;
        }

        // Check if n is divisible by 3
        while (n % 3 == 0) {
            n /= 3; // Divide n by 3
        }

        // If n is now 1, then it is a power of 3
        return n == 1;
    }
}
```

This function first checks if `n` is less than or equal to 0, since powers of 3 are positive integers greater than zero. Then, it uses a loop to repeatedly divide `n` by 3 until it becomes 1. At this point, `n` must be exactly 1, which means it is a power of 3. The function returns `true`, otherwise it returns `false`.

The time complexity of this algorithm is O(log n), as we're dividing `n` by 3 in each iteration until we reach 1.

